-- title:
--   Flat-at-p twin of a Hecke–Galois datum
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a level $N \ge 1$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers; let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal) of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of cusp forms of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $T$ be a noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with $\mathcal{O} \to T$ local and $T$ finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Assume $p \ne 2$, that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, that $p \nmid N$, that $p \in S$ and that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$. Given a datum $H$ of type [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N S 𝒪 θ T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8), that is: a ring homomorphism $\pi : \mathbb{T} \to T$ reducing to $\theta$ modulo the maximal ideal, with $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{im}\pi] = T$, such that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued character of $\mathbb{T}$ lifting $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ by an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T \to \mathcal{O}$, with $\mathcal{O} \to T \to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ surjective, together with a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible, the conclusion asserts the existence of a second such datum $H'$ with $H'.\pi = H.\pi$ whose representation satisfies `IsFlatAt p`: the residue field of $T$ is finite, and for every ideal $I$ of $T$ with $T/I$ finite the finite-level quotient $\rho.V/(I \cdot \rho.V)$ is, compatibly with the Galois action, the group of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points (with convolution product) of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ of rationals with denominator prime to $p$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Hecke-algebra-valued $p$-adic representation attached to a datum can be chosen (keeping the same Hecke structure map $\pi$) so that all its finite-level quotients at the prime $p$ away from the level come from finite flat commutative group schemes over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ — the finite flat condition imposed at $p$ in the deformation-theoretic setting. It is used by [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset).
